 "status_notes": "Final ICD applicable to S2K53, S2K531 and S2k54, a consolidated version merging parallel changes from s2k52, s2k53, s2k531 and s2k4.51 (change log, p. 6). Digitally signed in August 2010 (p. 2). Superseded by version 7.0 (11/08/2017) according to the change log of icd-7-0-final (p. 6).",
 "summary": "Version 6.9 (July 2010) of the SCOS-2000 Database Import ICD (EGOS-MCS-S2K-ICD-0001), the consolidated, signed issue that follows the 6.7 drafts. It is the final ICD for SCOS-2000 releases 5.3, 5.3.1 and 5.4 and merges changes made in parallel on several release lines. This copy comes from an archive.org mirror.\n\nIts structure is the same as 6.7. Chapter 2 covers file conventions, multi-domain installations and the FARC-based handling of sequences and displays. Chapter 3 defines the 51 tables field by field: monitoring parameters, calibrations (including conditional selection and logarithmic curves), limit checks, packet identification and processing, monitoring groups, displays, TC packet headers, commands with the optional dst routing table, sequences, verification, parameter sets, de-calibrations and range checks. Appendix A lists PTC/PFC types, Appendix B shows table relationships, and Appendix C covers PUS support by service.\n\nNew in 6.9 compared with 6.7 Draft A: section 3.3.2.1.5 on System Control parameters, where the multi-domain SCTL application publishes server-family status as TM through MIB entries generated by SCTLgenerateMIB; an optional per-stage verification window, CVS_UNCERTAINTY, which overrides the default window; CVE_CVSID and CVP_CVSID aligned to Number(5); a new applicable System Control ADD; and an updated reference to NIS/NCTRS ICD Volume 2 issue 4.0.2. Annex 1 is a cumulative list of document changes from R4.0 to 6.9. Use this issue when you need the 2010-era baseline used by many ESOC missions before the 2017 version 7.0. The visible tracked-change residue shows exactly what was edited.",
