 "key_points": [
  {
   "text": "Version 6.9 (06/07/2010) is the final ICD for S2K53, S2K531 and S2k54, consolidating changes from s2k52, s2k53, s2k531 and s2k4.51, with updated CVE_CVSID/CVP_CVSID fields and reference documents.",
   "pdf_page": 6
  },
  {
   "text": "The change log records intermediate drafts 6.7 Draft B (20/02/2010, SCR-3774/DCR-6008) and 6.7 Draft C (24/05/2010, R5.3.1, SPR 5504 on dynamic changes to TPSD).",
   "pdf_page": 5
  },
  {
   "text": "A new applicable document AD-6 (ADD-0022, SCOS-2000 System Control ADD) is added.",
   "pdf_page": 18
  },
  {
   "text": "RD-18 is now 'ICD NIS/NCTRS Volume 2 – MCS I/F', issue 4.0.2, November 2009 (version 6.7 Draft A cited 'NCTRA-NIS/MCS ICD Volume 2', issue 3.1, July 2005).",
   "pdf_page": 20
  },
  {
   "text": "PCF has 23 fields, ending with PCF_CORR, PCF_OBTID, PCF_DARC and PCF_ENDIAN; PCF_DESCR is Char(24).",
   "pdf_page": 40
  },
  {
   "text": "New section 3.3.2.1.5: the multi-domain System Control application (SCTL) starts, stops and monitors SCOS-2000 server families and stores status changes as TM packets; the tool SCTLgenerateMIB adds default PLF, PID, TPCF, OCF, OCP, TXF/TXP, DPF and DPC entries before SCTL first runs.",
   "pdf_page": 61
  },
  {
   "text": "CVS gains an optional seventh field CVS_UNCERTAINTY (Number(5), default -1) giving a stage-specific verification window that replaces the default (S2K-SCR-3774).",
   "pdf_page": 186
  },
  {
   "text": "CVE_CVSID and CVP_CVSID are aligned to Number(5), matching CVS_ID (S2K-DCR-3909).",
   "pdf_page": 250
  },
  {
   "text": "Unix-format absolute time (PTC=9, PFC=30, 8 octets) is listed in Appendix A as a type not defined in the PUS.",
   "pdf_page": 212
  },
  {
   "text": "Appendix C (PUS support) states that SCOS-2000 can encode and decode all PUS packet types and subtypes within the data-type limits, and details special processing for services 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18 and 19.",
   "pdf_page": 227
  },
  {
   "text": "Annex 1 groups changes by release: all evolution releases, R4.0 (6.0), R4.1 (6.2/6.3), R5.0 (6.4/6.5), R4.2 (6.5), clarifications in 6.6, R5.2 (6.7) and 6.9.",
   "pdf_page": 234
  }
 ],
